    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0354" n="240" xml:id="pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/45: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-07T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 7,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 7—3:40
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. Your 474, December 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d177-f1"/> The French
                    Government has given permission for facilities requested by the
                        Department.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d177-f2"/> I am transmitting copy of note
                    received from the Foreign Office in pouch tomorrow.<anchor n="16"
                        xml:id="d177-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d177-f1" n="14" xml:id="d177-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 92, <ref target="#pg232">p. 232</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d177-f2" n="15" xml:id="d177-f2-content">
                <p>On Apr. 8, 6 p.m., the Ambassador telegraphed that the French Government had
                    requested the Governor General of Syria to waive photographic restrictions in
                    the mandated territory (file no. 811.2300/88).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d177-f3" n="16" xml:id="d177-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
